  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the retrieval:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain**\n- `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 `get_request_handler`: reads raw body, negotiates Content-Type (`application/json` vs form), does `json.loads`, calls into dependency solving.\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `solve_dependencies` \u2192 `request_body_to_args`: maps the parsed body dict onto Pydantic model fields, handles the single-body-param \"alias omitted\" embedding logic, `None`/missing-vs-default handling, sequence/file fields.\n- `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v1/v2 shim (`ModelField.validate`, `field_annotation_is_scalar`, `field_annotation_is_complex`) \u2014 governs how nested models and unions are detected and validated.\n- `fastapi/params.py`, `fastapi/dependencies/models.py`, `fastapi/exceptions.py`/`exception_handlers.py` \u2014 `Body()` field defaults/embed flag, `Dependant` body_params, and the `RequestValidationError`\u2192422 path.\n- `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, relevant for how FastAPI itself would re-serialize nested models (asymmetric with what it expects on input).\n\n**httpx request encoding chain**\n- `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_json`/`encode_request`: plain `json.dumps`, sets `Content-Type: application/json`, no Pydantic-aware nested/union handling.\n- `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__`/`_prepare`: header negotiation, auto `Content-Length`/`Host`.\n- `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 `build_request`, where user-supplied `json=`/`data=` flows in.\n- `httpx/_types.py`, `httpx/_multipart.py`, `httpx/_utils.py` \u2014 type aliases for `RequestData`/`RequestContent`, multipart nested-dict encoding, `primitive_value_to_str` (how `None`/bools/numbers get stringified for form data \u2014 a likely drift point vs Pydantic's JSON `None` handling).\n\nThese are the files needed to trace both sides of the contract and write the drift analysis.",
